From 297c5a0e2fc5d3b4460393494368b8858a6c3a72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brhett <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:40:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 38/42] Finder: Google Drive, built on a bundled rclone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

rclone v1.75.2 is now a submodule (3rdparty/rclone). When Go is
available, CMake builds it and installs it privately under
libexec/finder; otherwise Finder falls back to a system rclone.

FinderCloud signs in with `rclone authorize drive`. Finder opens
Google's page itself and shows its own result page, and the token goes
straight into ~/.config/finder/rclone.conf (owner-only) without ever
being printed. A Finder-written systemd user service mounts the drive
at ~/Google Drive with a full VFS cache. Finder follows uploads,
downloads and failed uploads through rclone's remote control API on a
unix socket, and it notices when Google signs the account out.

In the sidebar, Google Drive sits under Locations after AirDrop, with a
spinner while syncing and a badge when it needs the user. Its menu
offers Sign In Again, Open Google Drive on the Web and Disconnect, which
stops the mount, clears the cache and revokes the token. "Connect Google
Drive…" is in the "…" menu and the sidebar's empty-area menu.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
